{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>From the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esav.</b> If he had said only <b>from the hand of my brother</b>, it would imply my relatives, and he is not a brother; therefore he said <b>from the hand of Esav.</b> And if he had said only <b>from the hand of Esav</b>, it implies any Esav in the world; therefore he said <b>from the hand of my brother and from the hand of Esav.</b>" "<b>Lest he come and strike me.</b> And how will the promise of ושמתי את זרעך be fulfilled? Another interpretation: he was not afraid lest he be killed, for HaShem had promised him ושמרתיך בכל אשר תלך. Rather, he was afraid lest Esav kill his wives and his children, and that is what is written: <b>אם על בנים</b> — the mother together with the children, like the additional offering on the regular burnt-offering. Regarding which it says ישרף, it is burned."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The last two sentences are textually obscure; the comparison of אם על בנים (Num 23:24) to עולת התמיד and the word ישרף (from Num 23:25, written in the lemma as ישרוף) are translated hyper-literally as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:05.382723573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}